  "title": "Per-agent launch overrides for reviewers",
  "summary": "Adds an `[agents.launch.<name>]` table to `osf.toml` so an adopter can replace a reviewer agent's launch command and add non-secret environment without forking osf. `agents::resolve` validates each override (known and enabled agent, non-empty command, no provider credential variable in any letter case) and stores it on the `Selection`; `reviewers::roster` threads the template into each `Reviewer`, and `prepare_command` applies the template env before the fresh run home and allow-listed variables so those always win. Only reviewer runs consume the override today; the builder platform and `osf agents list` are documented as following later.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
